            ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ildjc3f9fuKWQcHtt"><p>.02</p></div
            ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iLc5GW9IFerYk8sRh"
              ><p>🔁 <strong>Cravings Are Just Habits, Not Needs</strong></p></div
            ></div
          ><div class="iFmSzybgAXgthvzua" data-instant-type="container"
            ><div class="iSd6Q85qTllUz7iDa" data-instant-type="container"
              ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iwdxkqUnqiHU7Iz8s"
                ><p>You don’t crave nicotine like you crave food or water. You crave it because your brain has linked it to routines, coffee breaks, stress, boredom. Cravings aren’t pain; they’re patterns.</p><p></p><p><strong>Break the routine, and the craving loses power. Keep the ritual, change the substance, that’s where tools like Lio® help.</strong></p></div
              ><a class="iVKxJzxKDL2b7AYFg" data-instant-type="container" href="#iQhx8PxWpV45LjhSG" data-instant-action-type="scroll-to-section" data-instant-action-id="Qhx8PxWpV45LjhSG"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ifdF8mBGSPN6HLIWg"
                  ><p><strong>Next Reason </strong></p></div
                ><div class="iJKcWjoo1kDqf6o7D" data-instant-type="container"
                  ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="ivcBI89APMzXQ1hQO">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
