              ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iVEQwO9lmRulTcMRs"
                ><p>Many people try to quit slowly, smoking less, spacing it out. But that only makes the remaining cigarettes feel more important, more &#8220;earned.&#8221; It keeps the addiction alive and well-fed.</p><p></p><p><strong>Quitting fully, with the right mindset, is often easier than dragging it out.</strong></p></div
              ><a class="iucXQLTjlFunHorGy" data-instant-type="container" href="#iDQcXNYmMbG4paxA9" data-instant-action-type="scroll-to-section" data-instant-action-id="DQcXNYmMbG4paxA9"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ik7AlxSEOVMw04Ez7"><p>Next Reason </p></div
                ><div class="iy7qNk5gM7Kccwmtk" data-instant-type="container"
                  ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iXJJldK2IiMzMQ1mL">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
